Yes, I've rebuild iptables:

# make install KERNEL_DIR=3D/usr/src/dir_with_patched_kernel PREFIX=3D

(empty prefix, to install helpers in /lib/iptables/, binary in /sbin etc.=
)

I've also examined logs and I've found there:

kernel: ip_tables: table screwed up!

This message is generated by mark_source_chains function in ip_tables.c.
I've compared this function with 2.4.22 version and I've noticed that it
differs. Also diferences haven't been made by any patch in patch-o-matic.

I'm going to check iptables 1.2.9 and kernel 2.4.23 without any patches -
mayby one of p-o-m patch messes it up.

